# CHANGELOG

## [2.0.1] - 2026-09-15

### Fixed

- Minor bug fixes and maintenance updates following the 2.0.0 release.

## [2.0.0] - 2026-09-13

### Breaking changes

- Standardized double parton distribution naming on `DPD` across the public API,
  source paths, and serialized formats. The API uses `ICDPD`,
  `GenericCDPDFactory`, `mkCDPD()`, and `dpd()`; serialized formats use
  `PDFxTMD-DPDB1`, `PDFxTMD-DPDH1`, `DPD-HYBRID-B1`, and `DPDNAT1`.
- `ENABLE_DPD` (default: `ON`) controls both dense and hybrid DPD support.
  Enabled builds require Zstandard and oneDNN.

### Build and packaging

- Added vcpkg manifest integration that selects DPD dependencies when enabled.
- Removed the unused Eigen dependency; OpenMP remains optional.
- Improved Zstandard and oneDNN CMake target linking and installed dependency discovery.
- Fixed project-relative installation paths and restricted CPack setup to standalone
  builds so the library can be consumed through CMake FetchContent.
- Disabled builds omit DPD implementation sources, examples, and the concrete
  Python `CollinearDPD` binding. The DPD factory reports a clear disabled-support error.
- Synchronized CMake, Python, and vcpkg version metadata at `2.0.0`.

### Documentation and compatibility

- Updated portable CMake build/install commands and documented Windows/vcpkg and
  Linux package-manager dependency installation.
- Documented Python native-linking and DLL-packaging limitations.
- Kept all DPD serialized schemas at format version 1 while using `DPD`
  consistently in their identifiers; the separate `TMDPDF` API remains unchanged.

## [1.0.0] - 2025-7
- Full lhagrid1 format support
- introducing lhagrid_tmd1 for TMDs by extensions of lhagrid1 format
## [0.4.0] - 2025-6
- Uncertainty, and correlation support for collinear PDF sets

## [0.2.1] - 2025-2
### Bug fix
- Bug in reading multi subgrid lhapdf file fixed, also bilinear interpolation of the LHAPDF library is copied instead of my previous approach

## [0.2.0] - 2024
### Added
- Support for windows added

## [0.1.1] - 2023-10-01
### Fixed
- Bug fixes related to the PDF set downloader.
- Improved installation process for easier setup.
- Removed dependency on yaml-cpp to streamline the project.

## [0.1.0] - 2023-09-15
### Added
- Initial version release.
